 the  detection of cardiotoxicity  is obtained by echocardiography uh  this is something which is due to the  monitoring of the subjects  uh during or after the antrocycline  treatment  and when there is a problem with  um of dysfunction and  cardio functionality there is  the detection of cardiotoxicity but this  is something which is  possible to know only when the  hydrotoxicity and dysfunction is present  of course there are some markers that  are used actually but which are not  optimal the best one is caldectoponing  cadectoponin is a protein which is  present in the heart  the whole heart and functional arter  when there is cardiac damage troponin is  released  into the blood so in this case  if the subject treated with dental  cyclins have no  presence of troponins or notopaining  increase  we know that they are okay they do not  require  cardiac monitoring and they have a low  risk of  problems uh the problem is when there is  a positive  increase of troponin in the blood so in  this case  we know that these subjects are at risk  of  um sorry cardiotoxicity  uh but the problem is that that we do  not know  when and how much there will be  an impact of on their life and  cardiac function so the predict value  is low so we thought about micrornas  which are small non-coding rnas  they are transcribed into the nucleus of  every  cell of our body there is a long  transcript  which is present in the nucleus then the  the transcript is processed and cut  and it goes to the cytoplasm when there  is another processing  and the the end product is a small  21 to 23 nucleotides a single strand  rna which is then bound to a protein  complex  called risk which is the active player  in the function of micrornas inside the  cells  but but we were speaking about  circulating micrornas  so in this case the micronase they go  outside the cell they can be found in  plasma and other  human fluids bound to proteins or inside  vesicles  they're very stable because they are  protected from nucleuses  and they have been proposed as  biomarkers of several diseases  so we decided to investigate and  research  whether they could be used as biomarkers  of  ultracycline induced cardiac damage and  that was the aim  of our research so to investigate their  role in  cardiotoxicity  and here is our experimental design we  collected samples from  88 breast cancer subjects  these subjects were evaluated for  cardiac function  before the treatment with either  doxorubicin or a pyruvatin which are two  anticyclines and we obtained also  blood samples then the subjects were  monitored and treated with doxorubicin  and again  we obtained the samples during  the treatment and after the treatment so  we have three time points  here which is the baseline before the  treatment t1 during the treatment and  one month after the treatment and the  follow-up  which is three to twelve months after  the last infusion of the oxalobasin  so the aim was the identification of  circulating markers  of cardiotoxicity unfortunately  for us not for the subjects  not cardiotoxicity was detectable so the  subject suffered  no problems of cardiac function  so we had to do some rearrangement  of our research research and we into the  identification of the equality micronese  as predictive markers  of cardiac damage  the experimental design is similar but  in this case  we decided to divide the cycles into  groups basing on the presence  or absence of an increase of troponin  levels  in their blood and of course they were  also divided  on the base of treatment either doctor  will be seen or a peruvian so we have  four groups and then i'm  showing you some methods uh  for each some sample a plasma sample  obtain it from  the subjects we did a rna extraction  uh followed by microneedle transcription  which  is in a universal transcription every  microneed is later transcribed at the  same time in the same  um in the same tube for each  sample followed by  an operating open array 