tion  from for treatment with denturocyclines  there are different  anticyclines as i said before so the  clinician have to select  one particular androcycline and we  propose they do  a plasma microneed analysis  which indicates whether there is a  potential risk for these patients for  certain um selected ultracycline and in  the case of a potential  risk the clinicians could revisit  their options and select another kind of  drug  uh of course in the case of no indicated  potential  um cardiotoxicity risk indicated by the  micronese  the treatment crew continuous plan so  this is what we propose  to do in the future after our hopefully  successful investigations  but we don't um  we didn't limit our investigation only  to uh the the human  the humans we also tested an animal  models of dr rubicin this is a  quite um useful model  in which we took some mice we treated  the mice with doxorubicin for two weeks  and and then we collected plasma in this  case  because it was a study gain on  circulating macronutrients  and we collected plasma and investigated  cardiac function  um at the end of the treatment which is  um  after 14 days the t14 and then  also one week and one month later than  the end of the  treatment of demise so t21 and t42  and i don't know if it's  quite clear these are this is a picture  depicting  on the the function of the  three groups we identified so um we  identified three groups of mice  treated and untreated and some of the  mice  evidenced some real problems it is uh  the red box  and so there was a decrease in the  function of the heart  and so we again try to determine  whether we could uh see differences uh  on using unsupervised analysis so at  baseline the mice are all the same if we  analyze them on the basis of their  cardiac function  but then at t42 we see that the mice  are not all the same there is a group of  mice presenting  cardiac dysfunction which is separated  from  the other mice either untreated or  treated with oxyrubicin so there is a  differential response to the drug  and then we analyzed uh this mice  so we took the plasma from all the mices  and again we did total rna extraction  and uh open array analysis and and  to cut a long story short we  identified eight micrornas presenting  different regulation upon  treatment and the cardiac dysfunction  and so these are the results from the  three groups and  in particular we identified four  macronese which again we use to try to  to see whether they could identify a  demise presenting cardiac problems  between in the treated group  so again this is a presentation of the  3d clustering uh you can see that by  using  the expression of a restricted cluster  of micronesis we can separate  completely the mice treated redoxer will  be seen  uh when they are they are affected which  are the red  red dots so these are mice affected with  cardiac dysfunction and not affected  so treated with doxorubicin but not  affected  in their cardiac function we also try to  see whether this microorganism um  indicated  some problem and some separation in the  um these mice basing on their credit  function but we  didn't find anything which was  particularly useful  um of course in by  closing my presentation i have to say  some limitation of our  studies so known particularly as i said  none of the  subjects will be evaluated at any sign  of character toxicity  so this is a work for the future and  cardiac troponin was evaluated  using different methods because there  was a  multicenter study so we were not able to  correlate  uh troponin expression with microneed  expression  and of course another limitation is  limited number or micrornas  and also the animal models must be  refined this is a very  uh used quite useful animal models but  the mice  do not have cancer so it is not really  mimicking  um the the human situation 100  but we have future plans of course for  our research so  we would like to further evaluate uh  other subjects or human subjects to  identify  new micrornas which we would like to  analyze by next generation sequencing in  order to  look at many many microneed as many as  possible  and one thing that would be useful would  be an analysis in young  subjects suffering from cancer which  have a long expected  life so we would like to follow them in  time  but in conclusion we demonstrated that  circulating microneeds are indeed  good candidates as biomarkers to be  associated with cardiotoxicity and to  prevent hydrotoxicity with  possible future applications we  will go on with our translational  studies  okay in the end i would like to thank  all the people participating to  this project to this project uh in  particular the  monzino group with sonia matthias  veronica  really really a key person and  for the the recruitment of the subject  so magic  of course i have to also acknowledge the  funding agency  and i would like to thank everybody for  your attention thank you

